# What never needs to reach a build.
#
# deploy.sh does not actually use this file: it tars the context itself, with the same list spelled
# out as tar --exclude flags, because `gcloud builds submit` cannot stage source with the permissions
# this account has (see cloudbuild.yaml). This file exists so that anyone who *does* run a plain
# `gcloud builds submit .` gets the same context, and it is the third copy of the list alongside
# .dockerignore and deploy.sh. Keep the three in step.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which would exclude nothing useful and include
# .git — several hundred megabytes of history for a build that only needs the checkout.
#
# .cargo/ is excluded here as well as in .dockerignore, belt and braces: it pins an absolute host
# target-dir that breaks the build inside a container. See .dockerignore for the full story.
.cargo/
.git/
.gitignore
target/
out/
bench/
tests/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
